commit = transaction begin -> commit acknowledged; e2e = input scheduled send -> committed output consumed (ms); cores = system processes summed over 3 nodes (Redpanda: shards busy); verify = every input id in out exactly once (miss/dup) or still unprocessed in in (pend)
durability kafka: RF 3, min.insync.replicas 2, acks=all (idempotent + transactional producers), NO fsync (page cache, Kafka's production model); transaction state log RF 3 / min ISR 2; transactions v2 (KIP-890); read_committed
durability pulsar: E3/Qw3/Qa2 with journal fsync (ack after 2 bookie fsyncs) for data, the transaction log, the pending-ack logs and the transaction buffer snapshots; 16 transaction coordinators
durability queen: raft: 3 copies, ack after 2 fsyncs; one transaction = one raft entry (acks + pushes, all-or-nothing), the pop lease as the fence
durability redpanda: RF 3 raft, acks=all acknowledged after a majority (2 of 3) fsynced (write_caching off), idempotent + transactional producers; tx coordinator topic RF 3 (internal_topic_replication_factor); read_committed
